 "notes": "Approximate digitization; not supplied or endorsed by Eastman Kodak Company. Both page-3 charts are embedded raster images (no vector curve paths). Characteristic curves were traced at native resolution from column-wise darkness peaks after the chart's caption block, the inset time-gamma/time-fog chart and the right-hand curve labels were masked; the spectral curves with a centreline follower after the 1 px grid lines were masked. Axes calibrated on the printed tick marks (log H -3.0..+1.0, density 0..4.0, 250-750 nm, log sensitivity -1.0..3.0). Characteristic curves: one chart, 'Exposure: Daylight, 1/50 sec intensity-scale sensitometer; Processing: KODAK Developer D-96 at 21 C (70 F); Densitometry: Status M (Blue)', development times 4, 5, 6 1/2, 9 and 12 min with printed gammas 0.50, 0.56, 0.66, 0.84 and 1.05; all five are in all_curves. channels.k is D-96 6 1/2 min (gamma 0.66): the processing table gives D-96 at 21 C for approx. 7 min to the recommended control gamma 0.65-0.70, and the exposure indexes (tungsten 200, daylight 250) are stated for development to gamma 0.65; 6 1/2 min is the only charted curve in that gamma range. Densities are Status M blue, not visual; x is log H (lux-seconds) as charted. In the toe the chart shows three lines (12 min, 9 min, and one shared line for 6 1/2, 5 and 4 min, below about log H -2.6); the three shorter times are traced on that shared line, so their toe is uncertain by about 0.01-0.02 D. Toe tracing noise was removed with a running maximum so density is non-decreasing. log_h_ref: none. The chart carries no 18% grey, speed-point or normal-exposure mark, so no reference exposure is placed. Spectral sensitivity: 'LOG SENSITIVITY', sensitivity = reciprocal of exposure (ergs/cm2) required to produce the specified density; exposure 1.4 sec, D-96 at 21 C to recommended control gamma, diffuse visual densitometry. Two curves are charted, D = 0.3 and D = 1.0 above gross fog; channels.k is the D = 1.0 curve (mid-tone level), and both are kept in spectral_sensitivity.all_curves. rms_granularity is the printed diffuse rms granularity 14 (net diffuse visual density 1.0, 48 um aperture; D-96 21 C to recommended control gamma, tungsten exposure); no granularity curve is published. Not recorded (no field in this schema): MTF curve (page 2), resolving power (32 lines/mm at TOC 1.6:1, 100 lines/mm at 1000:1), time-gamma and time-fog inset, filter factors.",
